# The RAM tiers are symlinks out of the repository. Nothing in them is ever
# committed; they hold logs, builds, and scratch that is regenerated on demand.
tmp

# Deprecated temporary scripts are kept for exactly one commit and then removed,
# so they are never ignored -- they are supposed to show up in the record once.

# Editor and OS litter.
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# The browsable documentation is a **view**, not a source. Every page under docs/HTML
# is written by ./build-documentation from the Markdown beside it. Committing generated
# pages means every prose edit arrives as a diff of itself plus a hundred files of
# machine output. Run ./build-documentation to get them back; nothing is lost by
# their absence.
docs/HTML/*
!docs/HTML/.gitkeep

# Third-party code arrives through ./install-dependencies, which copies pinned versions
# out of the monorepo's shared library directories. What it copies is not committed
# here, because it is already committed there. The manifest in input/ is what is
# tracked; the copies are regenerable.
libs/9*
